From 7efb9e679a667c2f20ce7506fc99f7a7ac952f96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:55:12 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Native text: the game's text quads drawn as glyphs from a
 glyph atlas

Sharp text made a texture for every new text at the internal resolution,
the size of the game's TexImage times the scale squared (1 MiB at 4x, 4 MiB
at 8x for a two-digit number). Dissidia 012 makes about 24 new texts on
every step of a held list in its shop and accessory list, so the frame
stalled 60-130 ms on each step. Its text is drawn one quad per run: a
TRIANGLE_FAN of four through-mode vertices sampling part of the glyph
buffer as a CLUT4 texture whose palette is white with an alpha ramp,
modulated by the vertex colour, alpha test "greater".

- The renderer (Impl::native_text, from submit()): a quad of a glyph buffer
  that is an upright rectangle showing upright texels, with one colour and
  depth, modulated by its vertex colour with an alpha test of "greater",
  whose palette is one colour with an alpha ramp, is drawn as the glyphs
  that lie in its texels: each placed through the quad's mapping from
  buffer to target pixels (the interface's fit included), drawn from the
  font at that size (to 1/32 of a pixel per texel and half a pixel
  across) into a glyph atlas the first time, cut at the quad's edges and
  drawn with the quad's colour and depth, in its place and state. A new
  text costs no texture. Quads that draw nothing (no alpha, outside the
  scissor, no area) are skipped. Anything else is drawn from Sharp text's
  pictures as before.
- The atlas: two pages, 2048 pixels square up to 4x and 4096 above; new
  glyphs are staged in the frame's upload ring and copied ahead of the
  frame's commands (record_glyph_uploads() from frame_batch()). A full
  page is replaced by the other once no frame drew from it for six
  recorded frames (frames in flight and frame interpolation's replays);
  until then new text is drawn from pictures. A new font clears both.
- fonts::glyph_list(): the glyphs of the buffer a texture lies in, under
  Sharp text's checks (shared with sharp_text(), now checked_buffer()).
- fonts::place() and fonts::render_at(): where a glyph the game placed has
  its outline's origin in the buffer, and the outline drawn at any scale
  with a subpixel shift and the 1x glyph's emboldening.
- <PREFIX>_NO_NATIVE_TEXT=1 draws every text from Sharp text's pictures, as
  before; <PREFIX>_TRACE_NATIVE_TEXT=1 counts every 300 frames what was
  drawn, skipped, declined and why, and the atlas page's fill.
- The descriptor pool has room for the two pages.
- docs/PROFILE_GUIDE.md: native text, its switches, and that a texture pack
  does not replace text drawn this way.

Tested on Windows (clang, llvm-mingw, RX 9070 XT) with Dissidia 012
(ULUS10566), test data only. The shop list held down and up at 4x: frames
over 25 ms 18 -> 0, longest frame 67.5 -> 17.6 ms, render time at most
69.9 -> 0.8 ms, 3304 -> 0 textures; at 8x 53 -> 0 frames over 25 ms,
render time at most 129.0 -> 0.9 ms. The accessory list: 9 -> 0. The
graphics tour's menus, Story Mode gateway, Old Chaos Shrine battle and
battle results routes at 4x with frame interpolation: every text quad
drawn as glyphs, none from pictures, no page switch, the replay check at
0.02%; captures against Sharp text's differ at glyph edges only. Fill in
a 2384x781 window: text where Sharp text puts it. With
<PREFIX>_NO_NATIVE_TEXT=1 and with text.sharp=0 the old drawing. The
port's tests pass. Not tested: Japanese text, text whose scale animates,
a font change while playing, Sharp text's pictures for draws native text
declines (none seen), Linux, the Steam Deck, Android, the framework's own
build and tests, another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
